codex
A more structural opportunity is the layout between bmm and the final output kernel. Current bmm writes channel-major, so the output layernorm reads one value per channel with a huge stride. For `B=1` I can ask `bmm` to write into an NHW-contiguous buffer via `as_strided`, then use a row-contiguous output kernel. I’ll implement this as a branch and benchmark it.
apply patch
